. Sometimes, it also includes items like drainage pumps, for which we need to supply power, as well as road information because they need to create side plans.\n\nOccasionally, if some of our major electrical equipment is located on the side—such as the city’s official website handling water, natural gas, and our electricity—then coordination is required for electrical communication or power-related matters.\n\nAdditionally, streetlights also fall under their coordination scope. So, when we work on street lighting, we need to coordinate with them.\n\nFor larger projects, there are manholes. In big projects, after the side work is done, many cables need to be pulled over long distances, which can be challenging. Therefore, manholes are placed at regular intervals so workers can access them to pull cables. Our power and communication cables must be reflected in the overall external line plan, which is part of their testing network.']

