th Tier 4 being the highest, requiring full redundancy—meaning all equipment must have backup power. UPS capacity is usually calculated based on load, though there are no mandatory standards.\n\n说话人3: 00:29:10 - 00:30:45\n\nElectronic equipment, such as system units, servers, control systems (including building automation and security systems), and electronic communication devices, typically require UPS (Uninterruptible Power Supply) units. Since UPS units with batteries are relatively heavy, special attention must be paid during design: if the UPS is not located on the ground floor or if the ground floor has a basement, structural load data must be provided to the structural engineering team.']

