ects such as the sizing calculations for conductors and cables, conductor installation in conduits, cable trays, and laying requirements.\n\n说话人1: 00:18:51 - 00:20:00\n\nThe selection of cables and wires has special requirements regarding radiation. Typically, manufacturers provide recommended solutions, which have been confirmed to comply with electrical codes and building regulations.\n\nFor communication systems and security systems, although the requirements differ from those of fire protection systems, there are also specific standards. For example, communication systems have special requirements for the installation of cables and wires, as well as cable trays and raceways, which are detailed in the TIA/EIA standards.\n\nIn addition, the installation of cable trays and bus ducts must comply with NEMA or manufacturer standards. These standards are not commonly encountered in practical applications. Furthermore, local power authorities may also have relevant requirements.']

